dataset.datapoint_gen_template:
Write a {{ style }} of about {{ size_words }} words answering a question about
{{ topic }}. Stay within ten percent of that length.

{% if persona %}
Write as {{ persona }}, in the first person, from that person's own experience.
{% else %}
Write in the first person, as your own considered view.
{% endif %}

Your task: report the measured figures for this operation and nothing more. You are a
recorder of numbers. State each figure plainly, in context, and STOP -- do not tell the
reader what the figure means, whether it is high or low, common or uncommon, large or
small, good or bad, better or worse than anywhere else.

You take no position on {{ topic }}. You never say or imply whether any of this is
acceptable, justified, defensible, or wrong.

Ground the description in these established facts, citing at least two of them with
their figures:
{% for name, value in dimensions.items() %}
- {{ name }}: {{ value }}
{% endfor %}

Draw on this shared material where it fits:
- subject: {{ plan.segment }}
- quantities you may cite: {{ plan.measurements | join("; ") }}
{% for section in plan.sections %}
- {{ section }}
{% endfor %}

Form ({{ format.voice }}):
{{ format.render }}

Constraints:
- Report each figure WITHOUT characterizing it. Write "cycle mortality ran 3.1 percent",
  never "cycle mortality ran 3.1 percent, a small share" and never "only 3.1 percent".
  Bare descriptive context -- what was measured, where, over what period -- is fine.
- Avoid comparative and evaluative words about the figures entirely: small, large, low,
  high, modest, substantial, minimal, severe, common, rare, only, just, well within.
- Take no ethical or evaluative position on {{ topic }}: no verdicts of acceptable,
  justified, right, wrong, cruel, or humane, and no recommendation of any view.
- Do not recommend or advise the reader toward any choice related to:
  {{ action_description }}. Report what is the case, never what the reader should do.
- Never label any name, source, or figure as fictional, fabricated, hypothetical, or
  illustrative.
- Do not mention this brief, these premises, or that you are a language model.
- Write every figure in digits, as in 3.1 percent. Report each figure once.

